# Files whose exact bytes matter keep LF in every checkout, whatever the OS converts:
# - the hub embeds its migrations and checks each by checksum (sqlx), so a hub built from a
#   Windows checkout must hold the bytes a hub built on Linux applied;
# - shell scripts run in Linux containers and on Linux hosts, where a CR breaks them.
*.sql text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
# - the compose file a Docker machine joins with is served as its bytes are.
engine/hub/src/machines/join/*.yml text eol=lf
